        "geology": null,
        "hydrology": "The site is located in the lower section of the Cruces river basin, specifically in a post-1960 earthquake wetland.",
        "soils": null,
        "vegetation": "Vegetation is dominated by evergreen species of the temperate rainforest such as Olivillo (Aextoxicon punctatum), Tepa (Laureliopsis philippiana), Ulmo (Eucryphia cordifolia), Canelo (Drimys winteri) and Avellano (Gevuina avellana). In some areas, the deciduous oak (Nothofagus obliqua) species is abundant, representing one of the best preserved remnants in the southern distribution of this species, with specimens over 35 meters high and about one and a half meters in diameter. In its entire extension, the abundance of climbing plants such as Canelilla (Hydrangea serratifolia), Voqui colorado (Cissus striata), Pilpil voqui (Campsidium valdivianum), Medallita (Sarmienta repens), Copihue (Lapageria rosea) and Botellita (Mitraria coccinea) stands out."
      },
